Provenance of the files in tool/pstack/ and the skills installed from it.

Vendored upstream content (MIT)
  Source:   https://github.com/cursor/plugins, directories `pstack/` and `cursor-team-kit/`
            (deslop only), at the commit pinned in manifest.json
  License:  upstream/LICENSE for pstack and upstream/cursor-team-kit/LICENSE for cursor-team-kit
            (both MIT; the copyright line is in each file)
  Installed files: .agents/skills/<skill>/, upstream/docs/harness/claude-code.md,
            upstream/agents/comment-sicko.md (the Comment Sicko brief for no-comments), and
            upstream/cursor-team-kit/LICENSE.
  The upstream text of each file is byte-identical to the pinned upstream file. `pstack.py status`
  verifies its SHA-256. The project overlay in overlays/ is appended after a marker comment and is not
  part of the hashed upstream text.

Repository-authored files (covered by this repository's LICENSE)
  pstack.py, spawn_guard.py, test_pstack.py, test_spawn_guard.py, overlays/poteto-mode.md,
  overlays/no-comments.md
  Origin: written by the repository owner for another, private project and adapted for DocBridge.
  The adaptation removed project-specific paths and text, translated the messages to English,
  and dropped the git-ignored local model override.
